xnu 0263: say who is listening to the digitizer

Every synced sweep dispatches digitizer events and no frame follows, but a lock
screen that is not animating draws nothing either, so the frames cannot tell
"the touch never arrived" from "the touch arrived and did nothing". backboardd
counts as a client of the button service and the log says so; print the client
count of the digitizer service the same way, on the first events and whenever it
changes, so one boot answers it.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
@@ -346,6 +346,17 @@
 };
 OSDefineMetaClassAndStructors(MondrianHIDButtons, IOHIDEventService);
 
+/* Print the first few, then only when the number of listeners changes. */
+static bool
+self_events(UInt32 events, UInt32 clients, UInt32 *logged)
+{
+	if (events < 4 || clients != *logged) {
+		*logged = clients;
+		return true;
+	}
+	return false;
+}
+
